<symbol type="1" id="171" code="701" name="Start"><description>The start or map issue point (if not at the start) is shown by an equilateral triangle which points in the direction of the first control.
The centre of the triangle shows the precise position of the start point.</description><point_symbol rotatable="true" inner_radius="1333" inner_color="-1" outer_width="0" outer_color="-1" elements="1"><element><symbol type="2" code=""><line_symbol color="7" line_width="467" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="5333" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="5333" break_length="1333" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="667" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol><object type="1"><coords count="4">-4667 2695;0 -5388;4667 2695;-4667 2695 18;</coords><pattern rotation="0"><coord x="0" y="0"/></pattern></object></element></point_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="1" id="172" code="702" name=" Map issue point"><description>If there is a marked route to the start point, the map issue point is marked using this symbol.</description><point_symbol rotatable="true" inner_radius="1333" inner_color="-1" outer_width="0" outer_color="-1" elements="1"><element><symbol type="2" code=""><line_symbol color="1" line_width="800" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="5333" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="5333" break_length="1333" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="667" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol><object type="1"><coords count="2">-1667 0;1667 0;</coords><pattern rotation="0"><coord x="0" y="0"/></pattern></object></element></point_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="1" id="173" code="703" name="Control point"><description>The control points are shown with circles (footprint 24 m). The centre of the circle shows the precise position of the feature. Sections of circles should be omitted to leave important detail showing.</description><point_symbol inner_radius="4000" inner_color="-1" outer_width="467" outer_color="7" elements="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="8" id="174" code="704" name="Control number"><description>The number of the control is placed close to the control point circle in such a way that it does not obscure important detail.
An option for heavily building filled map is the possibility to have a white border with 0.1 or 0.15 mm in width.</description><text_symbol icon_text="5" rotatable="true"><font family="Arial" size="7451"/><text color="1" line_spacing="1" paragraph_spacing="0" character_spacing="0" kerning="true"/></text_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="8" id="175" code="704.1" name="Control number, with white border"><description>The number of the control is placed close to the control point circle in such a way that it does not obscure important detail.
An option for heavily building filled map is the possibility to have a white border with 0.1 or 0.15 mm in width.</description><text_symbol icon_text="5" rotatable="true"><font family="Arial" size="7451"/><text color="1" line_spacing="1" paragraph_spacing="0" character_spacing="0" kerning="true"/><framing color="2" mode="1" line_half_width="133" shadow_x_offset="267" shadow_y_offset="267"/></text_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="176" code="705" name="Course line"><description>Where controls are to be visited in order, the start, control points and finish are joined together by straight lines. Sections of lines should be omitted to leave important detail showing.</description><line_symbol color="7" line_width="467" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="5333" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="5333" break_length="1333" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="667" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="1" id="177" code="706" name="Finish"><description>The finish is shown by two concentric circles.</description><point_symbol inner_radius="3333" inner_color="-1" outer_width="467" outer_color="7" elements="1"><element><symbol type="1" code=""><point_symbol inner_radius="4667" inner_color="-1" outer_width="467" outer_color="7" elements="0"/></symbol><object type="0"><coords count="1">0 0;</coords></object></element></point_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="178" code="707" name="Marked route"><description>A marked route is shown on the map with a dashed line.</description><line_symbol color="1" line_width="467" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" dashed="true" segment_length="5333" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="2667" break_length="1000" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="667" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="179" code="708" name="Out-of-bounds boundary"><description>An out-of-bounds boundary shall not be crossed. It shall be used for temporary uncrossable boundaries used for the course setting.</description><line_symbol color="7" line_width="1333" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="5333" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="5333" break_length="1333" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="667" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="8" id="180" code="1000" name="Title"><text_symbol icon_text=""><font family="Kohinoor Gujarati" size="17639" bold="true"/><text color="41" line_spacing="1" paragraph_spacing="0" character_spacing="0" kerning="true"/></text_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="181" code="708" name="Border"><description>An out-of-bounds boundary shall not be crossed. It shall be used for temporary uncrossable boundaries used for the course setting.</description><line_symbol color="41" line_width="1333" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="5333" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="5333" break_length="1333" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="667" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"><start_symbol><symbol type="1" code="" name="Start symbol"><point_symbol rotatable="true" inner_radius="1000" inner_color="-1" outer_width="0" outer_color="-1" elements="0"/></symbol></start_symbol><mid_symbol><symbol type="1" code="" name="Mid symbol"><point_symbol rotatable="true" inner_radius="1000" inner_color="-1" outer_width="0" outer_color="-1" elements="0"/></symbol></mid_symbol><end_symbol><symbol type="1" code="" name="End symbol"><point_symbol rotatable="true" inner_radius="1000" inner_color="-1" outer_width="0" outer_color="-1" elements="0"/></symbol></end_symbol><dash_symbol><symbol type="1" code="" name="Dash symbol"><point_symbol rotatable="true" inner_radius="1000" inner_color="-1" outer_width="0" outer_color="-1" elements="0"/></symbol></dash_symbol></line_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="4" id="182" code="709" name="Out-of-bounds area"><description>An out-of-bounds area. A bounding line may be drawn if there is no natural boundary as follows:
- a solid line indicates that the boundary is marked continuously (tapes, etc.) in the terrain,
- a dashed line indicates intermittent marking in the terrain,
- no line indicates no marking in the terrain.
An out-of-bounds area shall not be entered.
Minimum width: 2 mm.
Minimum area: 4 mm² (footprint 64 m²).</description><area_symbol inner_color="-1" min_area="7111" patterns="2"><pattern type="1" angle="0.785398" line_spacing="1067" line_offset="0" offset_along_line="0" color="1" line_width="333"/><pattern type="1" angle="2.35619" line_spacing="1067" line_offset="0" offset_along_line="0" color="1" line_width="333"/></area_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="183" code="709.1" name="Out-of-bounds area, solid boundary"><description>A solid line indicates that the boundary is marked continuously (tapeetc.) in the terrain.</description><line_symbol color="1" line_width="333" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="5333" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="5333" break_length="1333" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="667" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="184" code="709.2" name="Out-of-bounds area, dashed boundary"><description>A dashed line indicates intermittent marking in the terrain.</description><line_symbol color="1" line_width="333" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" dashed="true" segment_length="5333" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="4000" break_length="667" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="667" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="1" id="185" code="710.1" name="Crossing point"><description>A crossing point through or over a wall or fence, or across a road or railway or through a tunnel or an out-of-bounds area is drawn on the map with two lines curving outwards.
&lt;span style=&quot;color: red&quot;&gt;If underpasses or tunnels etc. are to be used in a competition, they shall be emphasized with symbol Crossing point (710.1) or Crossing section (710.2).&lt;/span&gt;</description><point_symbol rotatable="true" inner_radius="1333" inner_color="-1" outer_width="0" outer_color="-1" elements="2"><element><symbol type="2" code=""><line_symbol color="7" line_width="467" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="5333" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="5333" break_length="1333" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="667" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol><object type="1"><coords count="4">-2000 1267 1;-667 900;667 900;2000 1267 16;</coords><pattern rotation="0"><coord x="0" y="0"/></pattern></object></element><element><symbol type="2" code=""><line_symbol color="7" line_width="467" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="5333" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="5333" break_length="1333" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="667" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol><object type="1"><coords count="4">-2000 -1267 1;-667 -900;667 -900;2000 -1267 16;</coords><pattern rotation="0"><coord x="0" y="0"/></pattern></object></element></point_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="186" code="710.2" name="Crossing section, one side"><description>A crossing section through or over a building, wall or fence, or across a road or railway or through a tunnel or an out-of-bounds area is drawn on the map as a linear object, according to the plan shape.
&lt;span style=&quot;color: red&quot;&gt;If underpasses or tunnels etc. are to be used in a competition, they shall be emphasized with symbol Crossing point (710.1) or Crossing section (710.2).&lt;/span&gt;</description><line_symbol color="1" line_width="467" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="5333" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="5333" break_length="1333" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="667" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"><start_symbol><symbol type="1" code="" name="Start symbol"><point_symbol rotatable="true" inner_radius="1333" inner_color="-1" outer_width="0" outer_color="-1" elements="1"><element><symbol type="2" code=""><line_symbol color="1" line_width="467" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="5333" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="5333" break_length="1333" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="667" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol><object type="1"><coords count="5">333 0;0 0 1;-800 0;-1200 -200;-2000 -867;</coords><pattern rotation="0"><coord x="0" y="0"/></pattern></object></element></point_symbol></symbol></start_symbol><end_symbol><symbol type="1" code="" name="End symbol"><point_symbol rotatable="true" inner_radius="1333" inner_color="-1" outer_width="0" outer_color="-1" elements="1"><element><symbol type="2" code=""><line_symbol color="1" line_width="467" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="5333" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="5333" break_length="1333" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="667" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_